  The 7th-order contrast curve and the "punchy" look come from Google Filament,
  filament/src/ToneMapper.cpp, Copyright 2021 The Android Open Source Project,
  Apache License 2.0. Filament adapted them from Benjamin Wrensch's "Minimal AgX
  implementation" (iolite engine blog); AgX itself is Troy Sobotka's, as used in
  Blender.

Algorithms implemented from their publications (no code copied):
  - Sky LUTs: S. Hillaire, "A Scalable and Production Ready Sky and Atmosphere
    Rendering Technique", EGSR 2020; transmittance parameterisation from
    E. Bruneton and F. Neyret, "Precomputed Atmospheric Scattering", 2008.
  - Hashes: M. Jarzynski and M. Olano, "Hash Functions for GPU Rendering",
    JCGT 9(3), 2020 (pcg2d, pcg3d, pcg4d).
  - Orthonormal basis: T. Duff et al., "Building an Orthonormal Basis,
    Revisited", JCGT 6(1), 2017.
  - Droplet erosion: H. T. Beyer, "Implementation of a method for hydraulic
    erosion", 2015.
